# Movie Recommendation System

A minor Data Science project that builds a movie recommender on the **MovieLens 100K** dataset using three approaches:

| Approach | Idea | Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| Content-Based | Recommend movies with similar attributes (genres) | Cosine similarity on genre vectors (scikit-learn) |
| Collaborative Filtering | Recommend movies liked by similar users | SVD matrix factorization (Surprise) |
| Hybrid | Combine both scores | Weighted blend of the two |

## Project Steps

1. Define recommendation type (content-based / collaborative / hybrid)
2. Collect movie ratings and metadata
3. Preprocess data (missing values, normalization)
4. Exploratory data analysis on user-item interactions
5. Model user behavior using similarity measures
6. Build the recommendation engine
7. Generate personalized recommendations
8. Evaluate using accuracy metrics (RMSE, MAE)
9. Optimize for scalability
10. Document design and limitations

## Dataset

- **Name:** MovieLens 100K
- **Source:** GroupLens Research
- **Location:** Kaggle
- **Link:** https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/grouplens/movielens-100k-dataset

Download it, unzip, and place the folder so that these files exist:

```
data/ml-100k/u.data
data/ml-100k/u.item
```

## Tools

Python, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, Surprise library

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv venv
# Windows: venv\Scripts\activate     Mac/Linux: source venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

> If `scikit-surprise` fails to install on Windows, install Microsoft C++ Build Tools or use `conda install -c conda-forge scikit-surprise`.

## Usage

```bash
python recommender.py --user 196 --top 10     # recommendations for user 196
python recommender.py --evaluate              # RMSE / MAE on a hold-out set
python recommender.py --explore               # dataset summary
```

